            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0166" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.61333/123.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Attorney General to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Justice</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have a note from the
                    United States Attorney in New York this morning, saying that Mr. Garver, of the
                    firm of Shearman &amp; Sterling, attorneys for defendant Sielcken, had yesterday
                    notified him that he would not press the motion to set the demurrer in the
                    Sielcken case for argument.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. W. Wickersham</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
